  "ingredients": [
    "2 teaspoons olive oil",
    "4 pounds boneless chuck roast",
    "1 onion, chopped",
    "2 cloves garlic, minced",
    "2 bay leaves",
    "1 teaspoon salt",
    "0.5 teaspoon freshly ground black pepper"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather all ingredients.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/_WKsRgWZMG64la5GyihNGHREkos=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/14621-beef-pot-roast-ddmfs-step-1-0751-4x3-21978522accc4e6791a2855878038e57.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/14621/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 325 degrees F (165 degrees C).",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Heat a Dutch oven or heavy pot over medium-high heat. Add oil, then sear meat in the center of the pan for 4 minutes. Turn meat over with tongs; sear for 3 to 4 minutes on each side. Remove meat from the pot.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/6Kahs279DWVR5O6AIuBiEoZkhoY=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/14621-beef-pot-roast-ddmfs-step-2-0752-4x3-e2543b3ed7bb4360906e890a4a121b48.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/14621/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Arrange onion, garlic, and 1 bay leaf in the bottom of the pan; sprinkle with salt and pepper. Return meat to the pan, place remaining bay leaf on top of meat, and cover.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/lDLJXs6ro-1qT1s410gDjY61G40=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/14621-beef-pot-roast-ddmfs-step-3-0753-4x3-a053a37d0a6d4faea7a97687e0603aa2.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/14621/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook in the preheated oven for 30 minutes. Reduce heat to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C) and continue cooking until tender, about 1 ½ hours more. An instant-read thermometer inserted in the thickest part of the roast should read 145 degrees F (65 degrees C).",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/9uOHFDf9Ymx8eATf5KNC9XIg1kQ=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/14621-beef-pot-roast-ddmfs-step-4-0778-4x3-1b1e9dfc167c404f85eff5c52f316e8d.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/14621/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Transfer roast to a platter and let rest for 10 to 15 minutes. Slice and top with gravy.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/46jdSnzZs5s0I1UAEi6m20cBDMY=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/14621-beef-pot-roast-DDMFS-4x3-13d65566a0774f4fa99f948381e085ca.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/14621/step_06.webp"
    }
  ],
